{"id":"d-01","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"In many countries, large amounts of food are thrown away by shops and households every day. Why does this happen, and what can be done to reduce it?","text":"Nowadays a lot of food are thrown away by shops and families every day. There are several reasons for this problem, but goverments and ordinary people can do much things to reduce it.\n\nThe main reason is that supermarkets want their shelves to look full all the time. When fruit and vegetables becomes a little old, customers doesn't choose them, so the shop has to throw them away. In addition, many people buy too much food in the weekend because big packs are more cheap. At home they forget about it and it go bad in the fridge. Another reason is that people dont know how cook with a leftovers.\n\nThere are some solution for this problem. Firstly, shops should to give food which is still good to a poor people or to charities. In France, for example, there is a law about this. Secondly, schools should teach children how to plan there meals and buying only what they need. Finally, people can use apps which helps them to share extra food with their neighbors.\n\nIn conclusion, food waste happen because of shops rules and bad habits at home. If shops and families will work together, the amount of waste will be much more less.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":23,"end":26,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"is","inserted":"are"},{"start":120,"end":130,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"governments","inserted":"goverments"},{"start":158,"end":162,"skill":"vocabulary.word_choice","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wc","original":"many","inserted":"much"},{"start":294,"end":301,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"become","inserted":"becomes"},{"start":326,"end":333,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"don't","inserted":"doesn't"},{"start":426,"end":428,"skill":"grammar.prepositions","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.prep","original":"at","inserted":"in"},{"start":463,"end":473,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"cheaper","inserted":"more cheap"},{"start":511,"end":513,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"goes","inserted":"go"},{"start":563,"end":567,"skill":"mechanics.punctuation","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.punc","original":"don't","inserted":"dont"},{"start":577,"end":581,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"to cook","inserted":"cook"},{"start":587,"end":598,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.art","original":"leftovers","inserted":"a leftovers"},{"start":616,"end":624,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"solutions","inserted":"solution"},{"start":665,"end":672,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"give","inserted":"to give"},{"start":701,"end":714,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.art","original":"poor people","inserted":"a poor people"},{"start":835,"end":840,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"their","inserted":"there"},{"start":851,"end":857,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"buy","inserted":"buying"},{"start":914,"end":919,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"help","inserted":"helps"},{"start":994,"end":1000,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"happens","inserted":"happen"},{"start":1012,"end":1023,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.wf","original":"shop rules","inserted":"shops rules"},{"start":1070,"end":1079,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.tense","original":"work","inserted":"will work"},{"start":1123,"end":1132,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"less","inserted":"more less"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p04"}}
{"id":"d-02","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"In many large cities, young people can no longer afford to buy or rent a home. What are the causes of this problem, and what solutions can you suggest?","text":"In many big cities young people can not buy or even rent a flat. This essay will discuss about the causes of this problem and suggest some solution.\n\nThe first cause is that prices grow very fast in the last ten years. Rich people and companies buys many flats for invest and then they rent it for a high price. Salaries of young people did not grow in the same way, so many of them spend more then half of their salary on rent. Moreover, in the capital there is not enough new buildings because building new homes is slow and expencive.\n\nThere are few things that the goverment can do. Firstly, it should builds cheap homes for young families and student. Secondly, it can make a special tax for people which owns more than three flats. Thirdly, banks could give a loans with low interest to young buyers.\n\nIn conclusion, the main reasons is investors and low salaries. If the state will build more cheap homes, young people will can live in their own homes.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":32,"end":39,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"cannot","inserted":"can not"},{"start":81,"end":94,"skill":"grammar.prepositions","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.prep","original":"discuss","inserted":"discuss about"},{"start":139,"end":147,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"solutions","inserted":"solution"},{"start":181,"end":185,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.tense","original":"have grown","inserted":"grow"},{"start":245,"end":249,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"buy","inserted":"buys"},{"start":261,"end":271,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"as an investment","inserted":"for invest"},{"start":291,"end":293,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"them","inserted":"it"},{"start":337,"end":349,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.tense","original":"have not grown","inserted":"did not grow"},{"start":394,"end":398,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"than","inserted":"then"},{"start":460,"end":466,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"are not","inserted":"is not"},{"start":527,"end":536,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"expensive","inserted":"expencive"},{"start":549,"end":552,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.art","original":"a few","inserted":"few"},{"start":569,"end":578,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"government","inserted":"goverment"},{"start":599,"end":612,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"should build","inserted":"should builds"},{"start":648,"end":655,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"students","inserted":"student"},{"start":674,"end":678,"skill":"vocabulary.collocations","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.col","original":"introduce","inserted":"make"},{"start":704,"end":709,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"who","inserted":"which"},{"start":710,"end":714,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"own","inserted":"owns"},{"start":764,"end":771,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.art","original":"loans","inserted":"a loans"},{"start":832,"end":842,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"reasons are","inserted":"reasons is"},{"start":884,"end":894,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.tense","original":"builds","inserted":"will build"},{"start":926,"end":934,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"will be able to","inserted":"will can"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p09"}}
{"id":"d-03","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"Many people today feel stressed by their jobs. What are the main reasons for this, and how can employers and individuals deal with it?","text":"Today many people feels stressed because of their jobs. In my opinion there are two main reason for this, and both employers and workers can do something for change the situation.\n\nFirstly, people have too much work and too little time. My friend work in a bank and she often stay in the office until nine in the evening. She told me that her manager give her new tasks every hour and she never can finish them. Secondly, many workers are afraid to loose their jobs, so they doesn't say no to there boss.\n\nEmployers should to hire more staff and to plan the work more better. They can also give workers an useful training about stress. Individuals can also help theirselves. For example, they can do sport after work, sleeping enough and turning off phone in the evening.\n\nIn conclusion, stress at work is caused by too much work and fear. Its important that companies and workers works together for solve this problem.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":18,"end":23,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"feel","inserted":"feels"},{"start":89,"end":95,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"reasons","inserted":"reason"},{"start":154,"end":164,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"to change","inserted":"for change"},{"start":247,"end":251,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"works","inserted":"work"},{"start":276,"end":280,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"stays","inserted":"stay"},{"start":351,"end":355,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"gives","inserted":"give"},{"start":389,"end":398,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"can never","inserted":"never can"},{"start":446,"end":454,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"to lose","inserted":"to loose"},{"start":475,"end":482,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"don't","inserted":"doesn't"},{"start":493,"end":498,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"their","inserted":"there"},{"start":523,"end":530,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"hire","inserted":"to hire"},{"start":546,"end":553,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.vf","original":"plan","inserted":"to plan"},{"start":563,"end":574,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"better","inserted":"more better"},{"start":603,"end":621,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.art","original":"useful training","inserted":"an useful training"},{"start":662,"end":673,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"themselves","inserted":"theirselves"},{"start":718,"end":726,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"sleep","inserted":"sleeping"},{"start":738,"end":745,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"turn","inserted":"turning"},{"start":750,"end":755,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.art","original":"their phones","inserted":"phone"},{"start":840,"end":843,"skill":"mechanics.punctuation","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.punc","original":"It's","inserted":"Its"},{"start":881,"end":886,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"work","inserted":"works"},{"start":896,"end":899,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"to","inserted":"for"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p14"}}
{"id":"d-04","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"Children today spend several hours a day looking at screens. Why is this the case? Is this a positive or a negative development?","text":"Children today spends many hours looking at phones and tablets. There are several reasons for this, and I think it is mostly a negative development.\n\nThe first reason is that parents are busy, so they give to children a tablet to keep them quiet. Also, games and videos are designed to be interestings, so children can't stop watching. At school pupils uses computers too, because many lessons is online now.\n\nIn my opinion this trend have more bad effects than good ones. Children who sits all day does not move enough and they becomes overweighted. They also play less outside and talk fewer with their familys. However, some educational apps can help children learning languages or maths.\n\nTo sum up, children use screens because of busy parents and attractive games. I think it affect there health badly, so parents should controlling the time what children spend online.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":15,"end":21,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"spend","inserted":"spends"},{"start":201,"end":217,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"give children","inserted":"give to children"},{"start":289,"end":301,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"interesting","inserted":"interestings"},{"start":353,"end":357,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"use","inserted":"uses"},{"start":394,"end":396,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"are","inserted":"is"},{"start":429,"end":439,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"trend has","inserted":"trend have"},{"start":486,"end":490,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"sit","inserted":"sits"},{"start":499,"end":503,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"do","inserted":"does"},{"start":524,"end":536,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"they become","inserted":"they becomes"},{"start":537,"end":549,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"overweight","inserted":"overweighted"},{"start":588,"end":593,"skill":"vocabulary.word_choice","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wc","original":"less","inserted":"fewer"},{"start":605,"end":612,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"families","inserted":"familys"},{"start":663,"end":671,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"learn","inserted":"learning"},{"start":782,"end":788,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"affects","inserted":"affect"},{"start":789,"end":794,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"their","inserted":"there"},{"start":827,"end":838,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"control","inserted":"controlling"},{"start":848,"end":852,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"that","inserted":"what"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p05"}}
{"id":"d-05","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"In some countries, people are getting married and having children later in life than before. What are the reasons for this? Is it a positive or negative development?","text":"In many countries people now get married and have children later then their parents did. In my opinion this is mostly a positive change, althought it have some problems too.\n\nThe first reason are education. Young people studies at university during five or six years and after that they want find a good job. Second reason is money. A wedding cost a lot and raise a child is even more expensive, so couples wait until they will have enough money.\n\nI believe this is good because older parents are more matures and they can give to their children a better life. On the other hand, woman who has a baby after forty can have health problems, and their children has less time with there grandparents.\n\nIn conclusion, people marries later because of study and money. Despite of some risk, I think it is a positive development.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":65,"end":69,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"than","inserted":"then"},{"start":137,"end":146,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"although","inserted":"althought"},{"start":150,"end":154,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"has","inserted":"have"},{"start":192,"end":195,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"is","inserted":"are"},{"start":220,"end":227,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"study","inserted":"studies"},{"start":242,"end":248,"skill":"grammar.prepositions","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.prep","original":"for","inserted":"during"},{"start":292,"end":296,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"to find","inserted":"find"},{"start":309,"end":322,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.art","original":"The second reason","inserted":"Second reason"},{"start":343,"end":347,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"costs","inserted":"cost"},{"start":358,"end":363,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"raising","inserted":"raise"},{"start":423,"end":432,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.tense","original":"have","inserted":"will have"},{"start":502,"end":509,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"mature","inserted":"matures"},{"start":523,"end":545,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"give their children","inserted":"give to their children"},{"start":580,"end":593,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"women who have","inserted":"woman who has"},{"start":658,"end":661,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"have","inserted":"has"},{"start":677,"end":682,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"their","inserted":"there"},{"start":720,"end":727,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"marry","inserted":"marries"},{"start":745,"end":750,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.wf","original":"studies","inserted":"study"},{"start":762,"end":772,"skill":"grammar.prepositions","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.prep","original":"Despite","inserted":"Despite of"},{"start":778,"end":782,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"risks","inserted":"risk"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p15"}}
{"id":"d-06","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"City councils should make all public transport free of charge so that fewer people drive into city centres. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","text":"Some people thinks that public transport in cities should be free. I am agree with this idea, because it can helps to reduce traffic and pollution.\n\nFirstly, if buses and trains is free, more people will leaving there cars at home. In my city there is traffic jams every morning and it take one hour for go to the centre.\n\nSecondly, free transport helps poor peoples. Students and old people often have not money for a tickets, so they stays at home.\n\nFrom other side, free transport cost a lot of money for the city. Goverment must pay drivers and repair buses, so taxes can rises.\n\nIn conclusion, I strong believe that free transport is a good idea, because the advantages is more bigger than the problems.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":12,"end":18,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"think","inserted":"thinks"},{"start":69,"end":77,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"agree","inserted":"am agree"},{"start":105,"end":114,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"can help","inserted":"can helps"},{"start":178,"end":180,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"are","inserted":"is"},{"start":204,"end":211,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"leave","inserted":"leaving"},{"start":212,"end":217,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"their","inserted":"there"},{"start":249,"end":251,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"are","inserted":"is"},{"start":283,"end":290,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"it takes","inserted":"it take"},{"start":300,"end":306,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"to go","inserted":"for go"},{"start":359,"end":366,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"people","inserted":"peoples"},{"start":392,"end":406,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"often do not have","inserted":"often have not"},{"start":417,"end":426,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.art","original":"tickets","inserted":"a tickets"},{"start":436,"end":441,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"stay","inserted":"stays"},{"start":452,"end":467,"skill":"vocabulary.collocations","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.col","original":"On the other hand","inserted":"From other side"},{"start":484,"end":488,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"costs","inserted":"cost"},{"start":518,"end":527,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.art","original":"The government","inserted":"Goverment"},{"start":576,"end":581,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"rise","inserted":"rises"},{"start":601,"end":607,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"strongly","inserted":"strong"},{"start":664,"end":677,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"advantages are","inserted":"advantages is"},{"start":678,"end":689,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"bigger","inserted":"more bigger"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p01"}}
{"id":"d-07","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"Some people believe that schools should teach practical skills such as cooking and managing money, while others think schools should concentrate on academic subjects. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","text":"Some people says that schools should teach practical skills like cooking and manage money. Others think what schools must concentrate on academic subjects. In this essay I will discuss both views.\n\nOn the one hand, practical skills are very usefull in the real life. Many young people doesn't know how to cook a simple meal or how pay bills. When they start to live alone, they make a lot of mistake with money.\n\nOn the other hand, academic subjects gives students knowledge which they need for university. Mathematic and science develops thinking, and many jobs requires this knowledge. Also, parents can teach cooking at home, so school don't need to do it.\n\nIn my opinion, schools should do both. For example, they can to have one lesson in week about money and cooking. In this way students will be ready for adult life and they will also have good knowledges.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":12,"end":16,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"say","inserted":"says"},{"start":77,"end":83,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"managing","inserted":"manage"},{"start":104,"end":108,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"that","inserted":"what"},{"start":241,"end":248,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"useful","inserted":"usefull"},{"start":249,"end":265,"skill":"grammar.articles","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.art","original":"in real life","inserted":"in the real life"},{"start":285,"end":292,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"don't","inserted":"doesn't"},{"start":331,"end":334,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"to pay","inserted":"pay"},{"start":383,"end":399,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"a lot of mistakes","inserted":"a lot of mistake"},{"start":450,"end":455,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"give","inserted":"gives"},{"start":507,"end":517,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"Mathematics","inserted":"Mathematic"},{"start":530,"end":538,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"develop","inserted":"develops"},{"start":563,"end":571,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"require","inserted":"requires"},{"start":632,"end":638,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"schools","inserted":"school"},{"start":722,"end":729,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"have","inserted":"to have"},{"start":741,"end":743,"skill":"grammar.prepositions","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.prep","original":"a","inserted":"in"},{"start":853,"end":863,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"knowledge","inserted":"knowledges"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p02"}}
{"id":"d-08","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"More and more employees now work from home for most of the week. Do the advantages of this trend outweigh the disadvantages?","text":"Nowadays more and more employee work from home. I think the advantages of this trend is more important then the disadvantages.\n\nThe bigest advantage is that people don't waste time for travelling. My sister spended two hours on the bus every day, but now she use this time for sport. Also, working at home give to parents more time with there children. Companies also save money because they needs less offices.\n\nHowever, there are some disadvantages. Some workers feel lonely and they miss theirs colleagues. It is also difficult to separate work and free time, so a lot of people works until late at night. Moreover, not every home have a quite place for work.\n\nTo conclude, although working from home have some problems, I believe it's benefits is more strong.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":23,"end":31,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"employees","inserted":"employee"},{"start":85,"end":87,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"are","inserted":"is"},{"start":103,"end":107,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"than","inserted":"then"},{"start":132,"end":138,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"biggest","inserted":"bigest"},{"start":181,"end":184,"skill":"grammar.prepositions","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.prep","original":"on","inserted":"for"},{"start":207,"end":214,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"spent","inserted":"spended"},{"start":259,"end":262,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"uses","inserted":"use"},{"start":306,"end":310,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"gives","inserted":"give"},{"start":311,"end":321,"skill":"grammar.prepositions","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.prep","original":"parents","inserted":"to parents"},{"start":337,"end":342,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"their","inserted":"there"},{"start":392,"end":397,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"need","inserted":"needs"},{"start":398,"end":402,"skill":"vocabulary.word_choice","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wc","original":"smaller","inserted":"less"},{"start":491,"end":497,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"their","inserted":"theirs"},{"start":582,"end":587,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"work","inserted":"works"},{"start":634,"end":638,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"has","inserted":"have"},{"start":639,"end":646,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"a quiet","inserted":"a quite"},{"start":653,"end":661,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.ss","original":"to work","inserted":"for work"},{"start":704,"end":708,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"has","inserted":"have"},{"start":734,"end":738,"skill":"mechanics.punctuation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.punc","original":"its","inserted":"it's"},{"start":748,"end":750,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"are","inserted":"is"},{"start":751,"end":762,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"stronger","inserted":"more strong"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p03"}}
{"id":"d-09","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"Many small towns now depend on tourism as their main source of income. Do the advantages of this outweigh the disadvantages?","text":"Many small towns depends on tourism as there main income. In my view, the advantages of this is more greater than the disadvantage.\n\nFirst of all, tourists bring money. They stays in hotels, eat in restaurant and buy souvenires, so local people has jobs. For example, my grandmother lives in a small town near of the sea, and in summer there are much visitors there. Thanks to tourists, the town repaired its old church and build a new park.\n\nOn the other hand, tourism can to make life difficult for residents. In summer the streets are crowd and prices becomes higher. Also, many young people works only during the summer and in winter they have not any work.\n\nIn conclusion, I think tourism is good for small towns if it is well organise. The money from tourists help the town to develop.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":17,"end":24,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"depend","inserted":"depends"},{"start":39,"end":44,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sp","original":"their","inserted":"there"},{"start":93,"end":95,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"are","inserted":"is"},{"start":96,"end":108,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"greater","inserted":"more greater"},{"start":118,"end":130,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"disadvantages","inserted":"disadvantage"},{"start":174,"end":179,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"stay","inserted":"stays"},{"start":198,"end":208,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"restaurants","inserted":"restaurant"},{"start":217,"end":227,"skill":"mechanics.spelling","severity":"minor","rule":"dense.sp","original":"souvenirs","inserted":"souvenires"},{"start":245,"end":248,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"have","inserted":"has"},{"start":305,"end":312,"skill":"grammar.prepositions","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.prep","original":"near","inserted":"near of"},{"start":346,"end":350,"skill":"vocabulary.word_choice","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wc","original":"many","inserted":"much"},{"start":424,"end":429,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"built","inserted":"build"},{"start":474,"end":481,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"make","inserted":"to make"},{"start":538,"end":543,"skill":"vocabulary.word_formation","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.wf","original":"crowded","inserted":"crowd"},{"start":555,"end":562,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"become","inserted":"becomes"},{"start":595,"end":600,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"work","inserted":"works"},{"start":628,"end":651,"skill":"grammar.sentence_structure","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.ss","original":"in winter they do not have","inserted":"in winter they have not"},{"start":732,"end":740,"skill":"grammar.verb_tenses","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.vf","original":"organised","inserted":"organise"},{"start":766,"end":770,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","original":"helps","inserted":"help"}]},"source":{"author":"claude-opus-5-5","promptId":"p08"}}
{"id":"d-10","set":"D","split":"dev","examKey":"ielts-academic","prompt":"Fewer people read printed newspapers than in the past. Why is this happening? What effects does this have on society?","text":"In the past many people was reading newspapers every day but now this situation is very diferent. People dont buy newspaper like before because we have internet and new technologys. I think this changes have some good and bad efects for our society.\n\nThe first reason is because internet is more easy and cheap. When people wants to know something about world they can just open their phone and reading news. They doesnt need to go to shop and buying a newspaper. Also in internet informations are coming very fast. Newspaper need to wait next day but in internet we can knowing everything immediatly. Young peoples are spending many time in social medias and they not interested to read newspaper.\n\nAnother reason is the price of newspapers. In my country for example the newspapers becomes more expencive every years. Why people need to pay money if they can read same news for free.\n\nThis situation have some bad effects for society. Many people who working in newspaper company can loose their jobs. Also old people which dont know how using internet have more dificult to get informations. My grandfather for example he always read newspaper and he dont like using computer.\n\nIn other hand internet is not always give us true informations. Everybody can writing something in internet and other people can beleive it. This is very big problem because sometimes peoples dont understand what news is true or not. But internet also have good things because we can read news from many countrys.\n\nIn conclusion I think printed newspaper will be less popular in future. Internet make our life more easier but it also bring some problems for people and society.","expected":{"errors":[{"start":24,"end":35,"skill":"grammar.subject_verb_agreement","severity":"moderate","rule":"dense.sva","ori